Introduction

Functional Reactive Programming (FRP) is a programming paradigm used to handle asynchronous data streams and events in a declarative way.

Simply,

FRP = Functional Programming + Reactive Programming

It helps developers easily manage data that changes over time.

Examples of changing data:

Mouse movements
Button clicks
Keyboard typing
API responses
WebSocket messages
Timers
User input fields
Scroll events

Instead of manually handling every event, FRP allows us to describe how data should react when something changes.